                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e2512df1-204b-45fd-822f-683b97aead90",
                        "source_entry_id": "3c8d3346-b46e-30d4-8567-080d0fd002e2",
                        "source_sense_description": "связанный с культом Вакха, вакханалией",
                        "target_lang_word": "bacchantisch",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bacchantisch",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ba427134-0509-3e02-b707-44e2968718df",
                                        "entry_id": "976ac0c1-26b0-3890-bd02-65b2dc5d1ea9",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "rauschhaft ausgelassen, trunken, zügellos"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "literary"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c2fb99a6-da63-41e2-9ce2-72cb10c0923f",
                                                "sense_id": "ba427134-0509-3e02-b707-44e2968718df",
                                                "text": "Gerade war er noch der tadellose Gentleman gewesen, bis eine dumme Bemerkung ihn in bacchantische Raserei verfallen ließ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6eaf7255-8ab0-47cc-8093-2250ade92a9b",
                                                "sense_id": "ba427134-0509-3e02-b707-44e2968718df",
                                                "text": "Die Studenten feierten am Ende des Prüfungszeitraums, vom Druck befreit, ein bacchantisches Fest."
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "62606380-b459-422b-b5c3-33b6fce6a7a1",
                        "source_entry_id": "3c8d3346-b46e-30d4-8567-080d0fd002e2",
                        "source_sense_description": "шумный, исступлённо-весёлый",
                        "target_lang_word": "bacchantic",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "bacchantic",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "57c3a929-4755-3f74-80ac-8fbafb86a5e6",
                                        "entry_id": "8c145cf5-c9cf-384f-9821-fa7f5eeb4a7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Bacchanalian; drunken or frenzied and unrestrained; orgiastic."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "7c37076e-fd3a-4065-ad8f-6e4aabb03571",
                                                "sense_id": "57c3a929-4755-3f74-80ac-8fbafb86a5e6",
                                                "text": "The orchestra played bacchantic music, and in bacchantic madness the dancers rushed by each other."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "102238a2-8c72-46ef-8395-50713756f0de",
                                                "sense_id": "57c3a929-4755-3f74-80ac-8fbafb86a5e6",
                                                "text": "There is a passage from chaos to cosmos marked by the \"bacchantic\" riots of Nature and even ourselves."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02755e91-7bf8-422c-8e9a-d544180b307f",
                                                "sense_id": "57c3a929-4755-3f74-80ac-8fbafb86a5e6",
                                                "text": "Yet nature is Spirit only in its otherness— self-alienated Spriit: \"A bacchantic god innocent of restraint and reflection has merely been let loose into it \" ( E §247z ) ."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ea32c67-0132-404e-a9cd-23e38449e697",
                                                "sense_id": "57c3a929-4755-3f74-80ac-8fbafb86a5e6",
                                                "text": "the reason for this was twofold: insufficient acquaintance with the metaphors applied to public life and, on the other hand, sublimation on principle of all erotic and bacchantic elements into mystic allegory."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a268caa0-2784-4c6a-a331-24aca76318ec",
                                                "sense_id": "57c3a929-4755-3f74-80ac-8fbafb86a5e6",
                                                "text": "Indeed the Tereus episode resembles the Hecuba even more closely because it combines the motif of a conspiracy of women (a motif also parodied in Aristophanes' Thesmophoriazusae, Lysistrata, and Ecclesiazusae) with the motif of bacchantic rage and collective violence . It is even possible that this bacchantic motif entered Ovid's tale via Sophocles' lost Tereus, though this is only conjecture."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "80e7174f-a8ec-3449-b8bd-c3f133d1a591",
                                        "entry_id": "8c145cf5-c9cf-384f-9821-fa7f5eeb4a7d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Pertaining to the clergy or worship of Bacchus."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "not-comparable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "108c21d7-85c9-449e-9622-511b6bbe9eef",
                                                "sense_id": "80e7174f-a8ec-3449-b8bd-c3f133d1a591",
                                                "text": "His friend Ted dancing the can-can trouserless with his shirt-tails flying, is an absurd equivalent to the bacchantic worshippers, who were supposed to don female dress during the rite."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5da42e7-7c60-42bd-9052-48a94828d32d",
                                                "sense_id": "80e7174f-a8ec-3449-b8bd-c3f133d1a591",
                                                "text": "In this way the spectators were contextualized as participants in a rite (the chorus of bacchantic dancers and those assisting were originally not separated, either spatially or in their pragmatic roles), who had to perform rite (rightly) that which lay beyond them all."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "681d4da3-9e27-4477-870a-94a3281a5735",
                                                "sense_id": "80e7174f-a8ec-3449-b8bd-c3f133d1a591",
                                                "text": "As am ecstatic city text it exemplifies the tendency to community, to festival, to love; and its bacchantic allusions remind us that Greek ecstatic religions were in part a protest against the restrictions of the urban, an effort to return to a more intense mode of existence."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e7d07881-0596-4e5a-a667-9b1cced4e95e",
                        "source_entry_id": "3c8d3346-b46e-30d4-8567-080d0fd002e2",
                        "source_sense_description": "шумный, исступлённо-весёлый",
